            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0377" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg253"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/780: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sterling</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-17T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                                1921—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>59. Your telegram no. 84, December 15, 4 p.m. This Government desires that in the
                    present negotiations between Peru and Chile, an attitude of the strictest
                    impartiality be maintained, and that you carefully refrain, therefore, from any
                    action which either party might possibly construe as a departure from such an
                    attitude. The Department has sent similar instructions to the Embassy in
                        Chile.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d207-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
